/* The limits, said on the front page rather than buried in the reference.
 *
 * A tool that changes a machine has to state what it will not change, and
 * the honest place for that is beside the pitch.
 */
---

<section class="boundary" aria-labelledby="boundary-title">
  <h2 id="boundary-title">What niwa will not do</h2>
  <p>
    It never applies on its own. The watcher notices and notifies; applying is your call,
    unless you declare a schedule yourself.
  </p>
  <p>Undo restores what the last apply changed. It is not a rollback of the whole world.</p>
  <p>
    One plan, in your order. Program order is the order; there is no dependency graph to
    out-guess you.
  </p>
  <p class="onward"><a href="/concepts/limits">Every refusal, with its reason</a></p>
</section>
